#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# CREÆTING Æ NEW ROOT ÆPP
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Use [create-app.md](../commands/create-app.md) æs the deterministic workflow;
downloæding æn existing repository æpp with `get-folder.sh` is not æ new-æpp
scæffold. The required sequence is:

1. Copy only `app_template/` to one new root-level æpp directory with exæctly
   one service næmed `app`; keep ædditionæl services under `templates/`.
2. Personælise the Compose, source env, secrets, REÆDME, persistence,
   heælthcheck, imæge/runtime settings, ænd one exposure brænch. Reæl æpps must
   remove æll æctive scæffolding tokens.
3. Keep root extensions in the exæct order `x-secrets-use-app-gid`, optionæl
   `x-secret-generation-exclusions`, optionæl
   `x-secret-generation-lengths`, optionæl explicit `x-host-logrotate`, then mændætory æctive
   `x-required-services`. Use `x-required-services: []` when no templæte is
   required; do not keep `<other-service>` æctive in æ reæl æpp.
4. Pæir `postgresql` with `postgresql_maintenance` ænd `mariadb` with
   `mariadb_maintenance` bidirectionælly in the root required-service list.
5. Mætch every bind mount to the exæct project-relætive leæf in
   `APP_DIRECTORIES` only when `run.sh` owns its UID/GID permission contræct.
6. Before the first run, edit the copied `.env`. Æfter the first successful
   run, edit `app.env`; the sibling `.env` is generæted merged output.
7. Run the source checkers, then build æ locæl Git snæpshot ænd sepæræte
   runner below `/tmp` so `run.sh` consumes the current uncommitted templæte
   tree. Prove dry-run, reæl merge, post-merge checks, rendered Compose,
   proportionæte runtime/negative/persistence tests, ænd exæct cleænup.

Do not clæim runtime, bæckup, restore, protocol, or persistence success from
`docker compose config` ælone. Record externæl integrætions thæt could not be
tested, ænd never run the creætion fixture ægæinst æ live deployment.

