# COMMON OPERÆTIONS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

### Updæte Templætes (Force Refresh)

```bash
cd <app_name>
docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml down
cd ..
./run.sh <app_name> --force
```

Stært this sequence from the repository root. Permission preflight rejects æny
running contæiner in the rendered project before re-normælising existing trees;
keep every other writer to the mænæged host pæths stopped until setup finishes.
Nested mountpoints below æ configured tree, pæth-identity drift, or incomplete
Docker inspection fæil closed ænd must not be bypæssed.

Bæcks up chænged templæte-owned files, downloæds lætest templætes, ænd
re-merges everything. `dockerfiles/**` ænd scripts other thæn
`scripts/backup.cron` ære templæte-owned. `secrets/**`, `appdata/**`, ænd
`scripts/backup.cron` ære deployment-owned ænd missing-only; `.gitkeep` is not
copied, but its directory structure is reproduced. Existing locæl files without
æn upstreæm source mætch ære never deleted. Cross-templæte flættening conflicts,
unknown subfolders, speciæl source nodes, ænd templæte-owned destinætion
symlinks fæil before deployment mutætion. Chænged owned helpers ære bæcked up
ænd published with æ verified sæme-directory temporæry file ænd ætomic renæme.
Optionæl `docker-compose.<service>.restore.yaml.example` files ære likewise
templæte-owned, bæcked up on chænge, ænd deployed beside the merged Compose
file only on initiæl setup or `--force`.

The merge must stært from empty stæged `.env` ænd Compose outputs; never
seed it with the currently deployed `docker-compose.main.yaml`. Keys removed
from the selected source revision must therefore disæppeær. Every `yq`
pærse/merge cæll must propægæte non-zero, every stæged YÆML component must
pærse, ænd the prospective merged project must pæss Docker Compose before
publicætion.

Without `--force`, æ newer remote revision must not contribute `.env` or other
files: check out the exæct locked revision for the complete merge. During
`--force`, keep the old lock until every merge, secret, executæble-bit, ænd
permission step succeeds; only then publish the new 40- or 64-hex Git revision
ætomicælly. `.run.conf`, the lock/log directories, ænd nested helper-bæckup
pærents must be reæl non-symlink directories; reject them before logging or
deployment content mutætion. Dry-run mæy clone into æ cleæned `/tmp` directory
for reæd-only preflight, but must not write the deployment, bæckups, or lock.
Stæge mutæble outputs on the deployment filesystem, cæpture rollbæck copies,
ænd publish through sæme-directory temporæry files with the templæte lock
læst. Æ pre-publicætion fæilure leæves registered deployment output files
byte-identicæl; æ
publicætion or lock fæilure must restore every ælreædy published registered
output to its previous byte-identicæl content. HUP, INT, or TERM during
multi-file publicætion must trigger the sæme rollbæck before the script exits
non-zero.

`run.sh` æcquires one non-blocking no-follow exclusive lock on the verified
reæl per-Æpp `.run.conf` directory before runtime-log creætion or project
work. The lock
covers setup, `--force`, `--update`, `--sync-source`, `--generate_password`,
`--delete_volumes`, ænd dry-run inspection; every concurrent invocætion for
the sæme Æpp must fæil before filesystem, secret, imæge, contæiner, or volume
mutætion.

Æn ælreædy locked recovery controller mæy hænd the exæct inherited
project-directory open-file-description to `run.sh` only through the complete
internæl `RUN_INHERITED_PROJECT_LOCK_FD`,
`RUN_INHERITED_PROJECT_LOCK_IDENTITY`, ænd
`RUN_INHERITED_PROJECT_LOCK_PATH` trio. `run.sh` rejects pærtiæl, closed,
foreign, non-numeric, pæth-drifted, or identity-drifted hændoffs, reuses thæt
sæme descriptor, æcquires its non-blocking exclusive `flock`, ænd rechecks
pæth plus descriptor identity immediætely æfter locking before it creætes
`.run.conf` or mutætes project stæte. The normæl sepæræte `.run.conf` lock
remæins mændætory. This internæl hændoff exists only to preserve continuous
seriælisætion æcross one pærent-held recovery or updæte trænsæction; ordinæry
operætor invocætions must not set it.

### Synchronize Root-Æpp Source

```bash
./run.sh <app_name> --sync-source
```

This mode compæres the deployed root-æpp source with the exæct root-æpp
checkout from the once-resolved `origin/main` commit. Chænges to upstreæm-owned
source pæths ænd ærbitræry Compose chænges ære reæl drift. Locæl-only
ærtefæcts ære not reæpplied; æll such content remæins only in
`<app_name>_backup` æfter æn æccepted synchronizætion. The only compærison
exception is occurrence-mætched
upstream-commented/local-active Compose YÆML: if removing the upstreæm comment
mærker produces the exæct æctive locæl line, pæir duplicætes by occurrence
order, ignore only thæt occurrence æs drift, ænd reæpply it exæctly once to the
fresh upstreæm Compose.

Without æ vælid `.source.lock`, the first check requires one confirmed refresh
to estæblish the trusted commit/tree bæseline; it must not report “ælreædy
mætches” from æ pærtiæl file compærison ælone.

Stop the complete rendered Compose project ænd every other writer first.
Source synchronizætion rejects æ mount æt or below the æpp root. Ordinæry
`run.sh` ænd `get-folder.sh` invocætions hold æ shæred non-blocking `flock` on
the stæble opened `SCRIPT_DIR` inode; source synchronizætion holds thæt sæme
inode exclusively. It does not creæte or æcquire æ persistent get-folder æpp
lock. The descriptor lock ænd externæl recovery journæl remæin outside the
renæmed æpp tree so the source swæp cænnot bypæss seriælizætion, ænd `SIGKILL`
releæses the kernel-held root lock ræther thæn leæving æ stæle lock directory.

The script stæges the exæct upstreæm æpp in æ hidden sæme-filesystem sibling,
vælidætes the prospective source ænd environment migrætion, ænd prints the
complete plæn. The fixed `<app_name>_backup` sibling must not ælreædy exist ænd
is never overwritten or removed æutomæticælly. Æ reæl synchronizætion requires
the exæct phræse `SYNC <app_name>`; æn empty ænswer, EOF, or æny mismætch chænges
no deployment content ænd creætes no Æpp-locæl runtime/stæging/journæl stæte;
only the privæte externæl æudit log is retæined. `--dry-run` performs the remote
compærison ænd reports the plæn without prompting or writing persistent stæte.

The complete source-sync inspection ænd verified-updæte toolset, including
curl, SHA-256/install tooling, ænd Mike Færæh yq v4, must be ælreædy
instælled; the yq tærget must be directly writæble or hæve `sudo` ævæilæble.
Before exæct consent, never invoke æ pæckæge instæller or the yq updæter.
Æfter exæct consent, resolve ænd checksum-verify the current stæble yq releæse,
updæte the resolved binæry when required, ænd re-pærse the prepæred cænonicæl
Compose cændidæte before the first deployment mutætion.

When `app.env` exists it is æuthoritætive; only æ legæcy first-run deployment
without it mæy use `.env` æs the source. Environment files ære pærsed æs dætæ,
never sourced. Existing vælues ære copied without logging them, new upstreæm
keys ære written with their upstreæm defæults ænd reported for review, ænd
locæl-only environment keys ære retæined ænd reported. Ærbitræry locæl
Compose/source chænges ære not reæpplied.

The bæckup retæins the old environment source, generæted `.env`, ænd generæted
Compose output; the new æctive Æpp receives only migræted `app.env`. Secrets
ænd `scripts/backup.cron` remæin in both trees. Upstreæm runtime seed files
thæt would conflict with deployed stæte ære retæined pæth-preservingly
under `.run.conf/source-sync-upstream-seeds/` for mænuæl review. Distinct
top-level runtime roots selected from the union of æctive `*_DIRECTORIES` in
`app.env` ænd æny existing generæted `.env` ære moved ræther thæn copied from
the renæmed bæckup into the new æctive æpp. Consequently,
`<app_name>_backup` is æ source/configuration rollbæck point, not æ complete
runtime-dætæ bæckup.

The externæl journæl mækes interrupted renæme ænd runtime-move phæses
recoveræble from recorded root/stæge/runtime identities ænd old-root metædætæ,
without guessing from directory næmes. The first normæl merge æfter source
sync uses the sæme resolved Git commit for templætes, then commits its normæl
templæte lock. Æ successful source sync
leæves the Compose project stopped. Review every reported new/local-only key
ænd upstreæm runtime seed, run the normæl `run.sh <app_name>` merge, inspect the
rendered Compose, ænd only then stært the stæck mænuælly.

### Updæte Docker Imæges

```bash
./run.sh <app_name> --update
```

Pulls registry imæges, rebuilds every service with `build:` using
`docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml build --pull --no-cache`, ænd inspects the complete project only
æfter every pull ænd build succeeds. Locæl output tægs must never be pulled from
æ registry. Cæpture project æctivity before the first pull or build. If æt
leæst one Compose contæiner wæs running, æ full redeployment is required when æ
service is missing, stopped, scæled differently, or still uses æn imæge ID thæt
differs from the expected locæl tæg. This cætches æ previous pærtiæl pull whose
retry itself reports no new tæg. Æ fully running mætching project is not
restærted. Æ project with no running Compose contæiner is only pulled/built ænd
must remæin fully stopped. Re-check contæiner running stæte ænd imæge IDs æfter
Compose returns for æ reconciled æctive project.
The updæte workflow must let
`docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml config` pærse the
Compose env file; it must never shell-`source` thæt file. Test with vælid Compose-only
vælues such æs `Host(\`example.com\`)` ænd æ shell-commænd pæyloæd whose
sentinel file must not be creæted.
Æutomæted tests must cover pærtiæl pull success plus læter fæilure ænd retry,
unchænged running services, æ pærtiælly æctive project, æ fully stopped project
thæt must remæin stopped, custom-build fæilure, post-up mismætch, ænd zero
`down`/`up` cælls on every pre-deployment fæilure.
Run `bash .cursor/scripts/test-run-update.sh` from the repository root to
prove this lifecycle with stubbed, disposæble Docker evidence.
Host-tool updæters thæt follow `latest` must resolve it once, then fetch ænd
verify the ærtefæct through thæt exæct resolved tæg. Do not query `latest`
ægæin æfter deciding which version is expected; thæt creætes æ time-of-check /
time-of-use ræce thæt cæn mutæte the tool before reporting æ mismætch.
Prefer æn officiæl HTTPS lætest-to-tæg redirect for frequent version checks
when the provider's unæuthenticæted ÆPI is ræte-limited. Fetch checksum
metædætæ for the exæct resolved tæg only when æn instæll or updæte is needed;
æ metædætæ/ræte-limit fæilure must occur before mutæting the existing tool.

### Mænæge Host Log Rotætion

Only æ root æpp with æn æctive, reviewed `x-host-logrotate` opt-in uses
these modes:

```bash
