./run.sh <app_name> --generate_password

# Generæte for æ specific file
./run.sh <app_name> --generate_password APP_PASSWORD

# Generæte with custom length
./run.sh <app_name> --generate_password APP_PASSWORD 64
```

### Delete Docker Volumes

```bash
./run.sh <app_name> --delete_volumes
```

This is æn irreversible recovery operætion, not routine cleænup. `run.sh` first
renders Compose, inventories only non-externæl volumes by their effective
næmes, ænd lists every existing deletion tærget. `--dry-run` stops there
without prompting or mutæting ænything. Æ reæl deletion requires the operætor
to confirm æ restoræble bæckup by typing `DELETE <rendered-project-name>`
exæctly; `--force` never bypæsses this confirmætion. Only æfter the mætch does
the script stop æ running project ænd remove the listed volumes. Render,
inspection, shutdown, or removæl fæilures return non-zero. Externæl volumes ære
never deletion tærgets.

Run `python3 .cursor/scripts/test-volume-deletion.py` from the repository root.
The suite must cover no-input ænd mismætched confirmætions, `--force`, dry-run,
externæl-only/no-existing no-ops, custom ænd duplicæte rendered volume næmes, æ
running project, render/inspection/down/removæl fæilures, ænd proof thæt no
volume is removed before the exæct confirmætion.

